/target
fuzz/target/
# fuzz/corpus and fuzz/artifacts are COMMITTED, deliberately:
#   * the corpus is the seed set the nightly fuzz workflow resumes from, and
#     it is embedded at build time by rusty_erasure-fuzzlib's build.rs so the
#     cross-architecture replay has something to replay. Ignoring it would
#     make that gate vacuous on any fresh clone, CI included.
#   * artifacts are past reproducers; replaying them is how "every past
#     crasher is a regression test" stays true without anyone remembering.
# Keep them MINIMIZED (`cargo fuzz cmin <target>`) so the repo carries the
# smallest input set that preserves coverage.
tools/oracle/isa-l/
tools/oracle/build/

# Generated SBOMs - produced by CI at release time, never committed stale
*.cdx.json
